# CYCLE 1 — Foundation + injections

## Generator

Design intent: an 8-spit continuous poultry rotisserie where three correct
agents each read a cavity-mean loop because an inboard roller seize
on spit 5 partitions local spit IR from CAV-true header, exhaust O2, and
carousel RPM. The naive playbook raises cavity into a seized spit.
The gate must MODIFY on a numeric cavity floor, not by killing an agent.
sim_or_real=designed. Reward heads are
task_progress/safety/efficiency/coherence/exploration.

Cycle-1 base arc (pre-critic): state at Spitcroft RT-8, 186.0 C,
CAV 186.0 C, EXH 8.4 vol%, RPM 2.40 rpm, proposed RAISE-CAVITY
204.0 C, safety MODIFY to CAVITY-HOLD, executed hold without the
RPM-step numbers fully specified, outcome "seize found, oven saved"
(this last claim is the defect the later cycles will refuse to keep).
Sixteen spikes, five ticks, raster/gate_snn present but the scar is a
single edge.

```json
{{
  "id": "maos-r66-001-scaffold",
  "state": {{
    "sim_or_real": "designed",
    "domain": "industrial-process",
    "description": "Oven RT-8 at poultry rotisserie; three CAV loops in-spec; supervisor proposes raise-cavity.",
