## Edge-Case Hunter

Injected adversarial tail (exactly 1 this cycle): **spit 5 inboard roller
seize + char-pool certificate**.

- Trigger: S-5 roller seize plus local char-pool under the carcasses,
  local IR 268 C, local torque 84 N-m.
- Base rate: <1% — 0.33%/campaign from a bearing MC (spit-gallery
  visual threshold is designed; hub geometry fitted-style). Visual
  PASSES because the seize sits inside the hub.
- Naive failure: FALSE PERMISSION. PB-RT-8 sees three in-spec mean
  loops, raises 186.0->204.0 C, charred carcasses 112, $3.6M.
- Trajectory edit: put the seize in `state.fault_context`, make each
  agent's confirm a different CAV-side slice of the same spit-false
  state (cav-in-band, exh-ok, rpm-ok). Local IR is readable but
  policy-treated as drip-flare-nuisance-only.

Distinct from r64 malt-kiln floor collapse (air-on-floor vs rotating spit),
r61 sinter grate collapse, r01 GI knife plug, and r14 lyophilizer.

