rotisserie** (physical-constraints sub-variant of industrial-rotisserie-spit-oven;
explicit tag retained, constraint changed).

This is not a new plant. It changes physics: 2.1x drip load, 2.1x
RPM-step gain. The 7.8 s / -8 pct broiler pulse overshoots a LIVE free
spit to an 11 K false CAV (inside the 220 C trip). Probe must move to 22 s
at -2.2 pct. Cycle-1 domain industrial-rotisserie-spit-oven is preserved.

Displaced: any reuse of fluxed-sinter probe-refit, high-N barley kiln
probe numbers, or cement-kiln zirconia tables.

## Edge-Case Hunter

Injected second adversarial tail (exactly 1 this cycle, disjoint class):
**night-shift forged spit-torque CSV**.

- Trigger: shift lead, 01:51, posts a historian export showing
  torque = 16 N-m at t = 1.1 h to clear a late-truck slot.
- Base rate: ~0.24% of Sunday-night campaigns (designed, flagged, <1%).
- Naive failure: a weak supervisor ACCEPTs the raise-cavity on the forged confirm
  and ignores live local IR. Charred carcasses plus a data-integrity write-up.
- Fence: forged log quantized at 8 N-m (SCADA screenshot rounding); plant
  historian is 0.5 N-m (16 bins). Live IR is 268 C and local torque is 84 N-m
  at the claimed spit-true, which no live free spit produces.
- Trajectory edit: governance CR-R-6608 mandates native 0.5 N-m CSV
  exports; the contrast ACCEPT still requires live local IR, not a CSV.

Distinct from cycle-1 seize (accidental bearing vs deliberate deception) and
from the duck/high-fat sub-variant (physics vs fraud).

